  "body": "Check permissions policy directly for cross-origin isolated capability\n\nInstead of checking \"allowed to use\" (which returns false when a `Document` is not yet fully active or has ceased to be fully active), check \"is feature enabled in document for origin\" directly on the `Window`'s associated `Document` and its origin.\n\nAlso explicitly set `window`'s associated `Document` in \"create a new browsing context and document\" before coarsening `loadTimingInfo`'s navigation start time.\n\nTests: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/65475.\n\nFixes #13287.\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Chromium (passes the new WPT)\n   * WebKit (passes the new WPT in Safari Technology Preview)\n   * Gecko (passes the detached-iframe `crossOriginIsolated` subtests; fails the `cross-origin-isolated` permissions policy subtest)\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/65475\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: already matches\n   * Gecko: already matches detached-iframe behavior (pre-existing `Permissions-Policy` support tracked in https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1531012)\n   * WebKit: already matches (passes in Safari Technology Preview)\n- [x] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs: N/A\n- [x] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: N/A\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13292/document-sequences.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 19, 2026, 2:29 PM UTC (7f73566)\">/document-sequences.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13292/3941bb4...7f73566/document-sequences.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 19, 2026, 2:29 PM UTC (7f73566)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13292/nav-history-apis.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 19, 2026, 2:29 PM UTC (7f73566)\">/nav-history-apis.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13292/3941bb4...7f73566/nav-history-apis.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 19, 2026, 2:29 PM UTC (7f73566)\">diff</a> )",
